---
/**
 * Termos de uso.
 *
 * ⚠️ POR QUE ESTA PÁGINA EXISTE AGORA. O plano de afiliado (pendência 12) lista
 * quatro coisas que têm de existir ANTES do primeiro link, não antes da
 * inscrição: mecanismo de `#ad`, página de termos, `/about` dizendo quem opera,
 * e meio de recebimento. Esta é a segunda. As outras três seguem abertas, e a
 * terceira é decisão do Bruno porque publica dado pessoal dele. (Feita em
 * 2026-10-03: `/about#who`.)
 *
 * ⚠️ E O QUE ELA NÃO FAZ. Não inventa entidade, jurisdição nem CNPJ. Onde o
 * fato depende dele, a página diz o que é verdade hoje e nada além — inventar
 * "operated by X Ltd" seria exatamente a fabricação que o resto do site existe
 * para não fazer.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RailIndex from '../components/RailIndex.astro';

const reviewed = '3 October 2026';

// Os títulos têm de bater LITERALMENTE com os <h2> do corpo — checagem 22.
const sections = [
  { id: 'what', title: 'What this site is' },
  { id: 'not-advice', title: 'Not advice, and not a tip' },
  { id: 'accuracy', title: 'Accuracy, and what to do when we are wrong' },
  { id: 'reuse', title: 'Using our figures elsewhere' },
  { id: 'links', title: 'Links to bookmakers' },
  { id: 'age', title: 'Age and responsible gambling' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to these terms' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use — mazetick"
  description="The terms on which mazetick publishes: what the figures are, what they are not, how corrections work, and how our measurements may be reused."
>
  <header class="mast">
    <p class="mono kicker">Notice</p>
    <h1 class="display title">Terms of use</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="spread">
    <div class="body">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <strong>Reviewed {reviewed}.</strong> Plain terms for a site that publishes
          measurements. If something here reads as though it were written to protect us
          rather than to inform you, tell us and it will be rewritten.
        </p>

        <h2 id="what">What this site is</h2>
        <p>
          mazetick publishes recorded observations of UK and Irish racing markets, and
          statistics derived from published race records. Every figure carries the
          instant it was true. Nothing here is a live feed: pages are built at a point
          in time and say so.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site is published by an individual, not a company &mdash;{' '}
          <a href="/about#who">the About page says who</a> &mdash; and is not affiliated
          with any bookmaker, exchange, racecourse or regulator.
        </p>

        <h2 id="not-advice">Not advice, and not a tip</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Nothing on this site is a recommendation to bet</strong>, a prediction
          of any outcome, or financial advice. We do not sell selections, and we do not
          publish a figure because we think it will make you money.
        </p>
        <p>
          Several of our own published findings are negative &mdash; that is, they
          record strategies that lost money under honest measurement. Those are in{' '}
          <a href="/research">Research</a>, with their sample sizes. Read them before
          assuming any number here supports a bet.
        </p>

        <h2 id="accuracy">Accuracy, and what to do when we are wrong</h2>
        <p>
          The figures are our own count over data we collect and over published race
          records. We check them, we publish the method, and we still get things wrong.
          When we find an error we correct it in public and say what changed, rather
          than editing quietly.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The site is provided as it is, with no warranty that any figure is
          accurate, complete or current.</strong> Collection can fail, a source can
          change its shape without telling us, and an archive can be thinner in one
          period than another &mdash; where we know that, the page says so. Decisions
          you take on the basis of these numbers are yours.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a number here looks wrong, <a href="/contact">tell us</a>. Corrections to
          measurements are the most useful thing anyone can send.
        </p>

        <h2 id="reuse">Using our figures elsewhere</h2>
        <p>
          The <strong>content</strong> of this site &mdash; the measurements, the
          articles and the derived statistics &mdash; is published under{' '}
          <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license noopener"
             target="_blank">CC BY 4.0</a>. Quote it, chart it, argue with it, in public
          or in print, as long as you say where it came from and link back.
        </p>
        <p>
          The <strong>code</strong> that builds the site is MIT-licensed and public.
        </p>
        <p>
          Two limits, and both are about the sources rather than about us. We are
          licensed to publish our own derived figures, not to redistribute the
          underlying feeds: <strong>please do not scrape these pages to reconstitute a
          bulk dataset or to run a feed of your own.</strong> And prices shown by a
          bookmaker or an exchange belong to them, which is why you will not find a
          price on this site.
        </p>

        <h2 id="links">Links to bookmakers</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>At the time of writing this site carries no paid links of any
          kind</strong> &mdash; no affiliate links, no advertising, no sponsored
          content. If that changes, every paid link will be labelled{' '}
          <code>#ad</code> where you can see it before you click, and this section will
          say so with the date it changed. A label buried in a footer is not a label.
        </p>

        <h2 id="age">Age and responsible gambling</h2>
        <p>
          This site is intended for people aged <strong>18 or over</strong>. It
          discusses betting markets, and betting can cause harm. If gambling is costing
          you more than money, <a href="/responsible-gambling">the help is here</a>:
          BeGambleAware, GamCare, and the National Gambling Helpline on 0808 8020 133,
          free and open at any hour.
        </p>

        <h2 id="changes">Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          This page carries the date it was last reviewed, at the top. Changes that
          matter &mdash; a paid link appearing, the licence changing, a new source
          &mdash; will be stated here rather than slipped in, because a terms page that
          rewrites itself silently is worth nothing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <RailIndex items={sections} />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
